            "action": "ANNOTATED",
            "changes": "Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/S6_Medium-edison-literature.md (local artifact — research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather than linked). Report verdict: **Recommended interpretation:** “S6 medium” is a **named culture-medium formulation**, not a single chemical, salt/hydrate, buffer molecule, extract, or generic medium-component family. The strongest retrievable lineage is its use as an **S6 liquid medium for *Bacillus subtilis***, with the formulation attributed to Fujita and Freese (1981). A later paper explicitly distinguishes S6 from tryptose  No ontology CURIE was proposed. Recorded as provenance only — no grounding applied from this run. Edison's recommendations are deliberately conservative, and a plausible identifier promoted by a mechanism that never decided anything is what #203 and #263 exist to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator's to accept or reject.",
